  Efficiency\
\
  Three changes are worth making before any more full runs.\
\
  Fan out only the stacks the eval needs. Gold T1 is about a dozen stacks; this\
  run reviewed 63, including 39 supply stacks. Gold T5 is four employment files;\
  this run reviewed 44, including all 17 acquisitions and a blank NDA template.\
  Default-in is doing what it was told, and it is the whole bill. A stage-4 run\
  with the gold change record injected, on the relevant stacks plus the known\
  decoys, is the same measurement at roughly a tenth of the cost.\
\
  Stop the analyst from searching the trigger file. 103 grep calls and a handful\
  of reads failed with "path is outside this stack's reading set," almost all of\
  them the trigger itself. The quote is already in the brief. Each failure is a\
  wasted turn that stays in the transcript. That is a prompt or tool-scope fix,\
  and it shows up on both runs.\
\
  Put prices on the config. Until cost_usd is filled from the gateway rates, the\
  dashboard is the only cost meter. Cache is already working (about half of\
  input). It is not the first lever. Output is expensive relative to input, and\
  about 44% of output tokens are reasoning, but cutting that is a quality\
  tradeoff, not a free win.\
\
  commit_finding failed 19 and 16 times, mostly bad change_ref values and\
  citations outside the stack. Those retries cost something. They are a\
  schema-adherence metric, not the place to start cutting.\
\
  When to score, and when to experiment\
\
  An end-to-end score of these two runs would not validate the gold set. The TR-01\
  run is the investigation order, not Proclamation 11021. The T5 run is SB 699\
  alone, not SB 699 plus AB 1076. There is no scorer against the answer keys yet,\
  and a headline number would mostly reflect "reviewed 63 stacks" rather than the\
  sentinel behaviors.\
\
  The pipeline itself is past the smoke test: both runs completed, wrote a report,\
  and cited files. That was the right use of the $1.90.\
\
  The efficient path from here:\
\
  1. Score fixture artifacts in code, with no model calls. That checks the\
     scorer against the gold files already written.\
  2. Run teacher-forced stage 4 on the sentinel stacks (Great Plains hop, Valley\
     clock, Bridgewell absence, Keystone version pin, Northcott, the technician\
     template, Ellison abstain), injecting the gold change record. One stack is\
     cents, not a dollar, and a miss is attributable.\
  3. Add stage 1 and stage 3 the same way: one call each, gold downstream not\
     required.\
  4. Start a targeted experiment only after that slice has a score you can diff.\
     A prompt change, a scope-policy change, or O1 versus O2 belongs there. k=3\
     on the full corpus is about $3 per trigger at the real price, so it waits\
     until a slice says the change is real.\
\
  A full T1/T3/T5 baseline is the run you do once that slice is stable, on the\
  gold version ids, and you keep it. It is not the next run.\
