  A teacher-forced run scores one stage on the correct input. A full baseline\
  scores the whole pipeline on whatever it actually produced. The harness changes\
  below make the cheap version possible.\
\
  Teacher-forced means the stage under test is handed the right upstream answer\
  instead of the previous stage's output. If stage 4 is given the correct change\
  and still misses the Valley notice deadline, that miss belongs to stage 4. If it\
  is given a bad stage-1 summary and then misses, you cannot tell which stage\
  failed.\
\
  The gold change record is that upstream answer for the legal change: the items,\
  verbatim quotes, legal status, and company gate already written in the answer\
  key. harness stage --stage 4 --inject change_record.json feeds it in and marks\
  the stage injected. The stack analyst never has to rediscover Proclamation\
  11021.\
\
  The two runs you already have are a wiring check. They finished, wrote reports,\
  and showed where the money goes. They are not a baseline. The TR-01 run read the\
  investigation order, not Proclamation 11021, and the T5 run read SB 699 only.\
  Nothing was scored against the answer keys.\
\
  The preliminary slice tests one behavior at a time: given the gold change, does\
  Great Plains cite the master-supply hop, does Valley see a live clock, does the\
  Keystone purchase order stay pinned to the 2019 terms. Each of those is one\
  stack and a few cents. A full baseline is the later run, on the gold version\
  ids, with no injected answers, scored end to end. That is the number you keep.\
  It is the wrong next spend, because one upstream mistake makes every later miss\
  look like a finding error, at about $0.90 per trigger.\
\
  Three harness changes are in place.\
\
  \'95 The stack analyst is told to copy the trigger quote from the change record\
    and not to open the snapshot. If it tries anyway, grep and read return that\
    quote instead of "path is outside this stack's reading set." That refusal\
    was 103 of the failed tool calls across the two runs.\
  \'95 A config field only_stacks caps fan-out. Omit it and every in-scope stack\
    still runs. Set it and stacks outside the list are recorded as out of scope\
    after the model's own scope decision, with that decision kept in the reason.\
    An empty list is an error.\
  \'95 configs/o1-glm.json and configs/j-jev.json now price zai/glm-5.3-flash at\
    $0.15 / $0.03 cached / $0.50 per million, so cost_usd fills in. Sonnet is\
    priced at the $2 / $10 rate from the design notes. DeepSeek is still\
    unpriced because the published range is not a single rate.\
\
  The tests covering the trigger reply and the stack cap passed.\
